================================== Bug Bounty Platforms =====================================

HackerOne (Largest volume. Most competitive. Good training via Hacker101.)
hackerone.com

Bugcrowd (Beginner-friendly. CrowdMatch AI matches you to programs by skill.)
bugcrowd.com

Intigriti (Strong EU focus. Fast triage. Less duplicate-heavy than HackerOne.)
intigriti.com

YesWeHack (Largest EU-founded platform. French/German/Swiss companies. Less crowded.)
yeswehack.com

Synack (Invite-only. Pass a skills test + background check. Avg $2k-$10k payouts.)
synack.com/red-team

Yogosha (European. Combines pentesting + bug bounty. Programs live in days.)
yogosha.com

Hackrate (Smaller. Cost-effective custom programs with advanced monitoring.)
hackrate.com

Open Bug Bounty (Completely free and open. No login required to submit. Good for beginners.)
openbugbounty.org

Immunefi (Dominates Web3/DeFi. Six and seven figure bounties for smart contract bugs.)
immunefi.com

HackenProof (Strong blockchain/crypto focus. Alongside Immunefi for Web3 targets.)
hackenproof.com


================================== Aggregators & Directories =================================

Chaos by ProjectDiscovery (Dataset of in-scope domains from ALL public programs. Not a platform - raw recon data.)
chaos.projectdiscovery.io

Bug Bounties Directory (3000+ active programs and VDPs. Community maintained. Has an API.)
bug-bounties.as93.net

FireBounty (Aggregates VDP and bounty policies from across the internet.)
firebounty.com

Disclose.io (Vendor-agnostic community directory. Includes contact, safe harbor, reward status.)
disclose.io

Crawler.ninja Security.txt Dump (Raw crawled security.txt values with frequency counts. Gold mine for unknown programs.)
crawler.ninja/files/security-txt-values.txt


